 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186273303 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275067 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186274341 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275067 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275067 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275067 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186272774 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275067 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f570cb94-97be-59e0-a398-fb3eb82d9321" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275327 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186275038 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275327 #edb/ref 1069 "q-15457" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275327 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275327 #edb/ref 1071 "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t),\\,y={cos}^{2}⁡(t),\\,0\\le t<2\\pi ,\n$$\n\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275327 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0d08529b-8573-5553-9a9b-ff64d66c71ec" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275327 #edb/ref 1074 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t).\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6},$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =-\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275333 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186275067 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275333 #edb/ref 1069 "q-15476" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275333 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275333 #edb/ref 1071 "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t})},\\,y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡({e}^{t}),\\,-\\infty <t<1,\n$$\n\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275333 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "18a41cc2-6786-5c7c-b54f-7a6c8dbb881f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275333 #edb/ref 1074 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t})}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡({e}^{t})\\cdot {e}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({e}^{t})}{2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t})}}, \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) & =-{e}^{t}{csc}^{2}⁡({e}^{t}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{-{e}^{t}{csc}^{2}⁡({e}^{t})}{(\\frac{{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({e}^{t})}{2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t})}})} \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t})}}{{sin}^{2}⁡({e}^{t})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({e}^{t})} \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{2}{{sin}^{3/2}⁡({e}^{t})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({e}^{t})}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}),$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =-\\,\\frac{2}{{sin}^{3/2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})} \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{2}{{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{3/2}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})} \\\\  & =-2\\cdot {2}^{3/2}\\,\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =-8\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186333819 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{{e}^{2}}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186333819 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186333819 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5acc6cd8-f001-5394-a6fb-c1dd0fc5b3b9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186334283 #edb/ref 1080 "{e}^{-2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186334283 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186334283 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "911bd715-c47b-52fc-8b17-1d94b494a8dc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186334450 #edb/ref 1080 "2{e}^{-2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186334450 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186334450 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a6a0b785-553c-5b96-8cde-3a695db73d7a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186334529 #edb/ref 1080 "{e}^{-3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186334529 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186334529 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "aef4e7d5-b6bf-5eef-a5a0-2697f1745f39" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186334694 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{{e}^{-3}}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186334694 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186334694 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c4b6f7ec-a4b3-53d6-a622-e814425b78ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335566 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186333819 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335566 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186334283 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335566 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186334450 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335566 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186334529 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335566 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186334694 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335566 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335566 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335566 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186334529 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335566 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b356f94f-948d-5358-9ef9-3fb6cfeb2cdd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335953 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186335566 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335953 #edb/ref 1069 "q-6816" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335953 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335953 #edb/ref 1071 "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx={e}^{2t},\\,y=({t}^{2}-1){e}^{-t},\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\n find the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335953 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "18b27deb-1f86-5103-a5ac-bd0f135dadc6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335953 #edb/ref 1074 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2{e}^{2t},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=(1+2t-{t}^{2}){e}^{-t}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{(1+2t-{t}^{2}){e}^{-t}}{2{e}^{2t}}=\\frac{1}{2}(1+2t-{t}^{2}){e}^{-3t}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=1$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{1}{2}(1+2(1)-(1)^{2}){e}^{-3(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1+2-1){e}^{-3} \\\\  & ={e}^{-3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403272 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403272 #edb/ref 1069 "q-6812" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403272 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403272 #edb/ref 1071 "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=({t}^{3}-1){e}^{t},\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\n find the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403272 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ef78af33-68fa-5c96-9f7c-05772b13cffb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403272 #edb/ref 1074 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=({t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}-1){e}^{t},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{({t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}-1){e}^{t}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=0$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡0}{({0}^{3}+3\\cdot {0}^{2}-1){e}^{0}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1)}{(-1)\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =-2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403273 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403273 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403275 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403273 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403276 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403273 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403277 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403273 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403278 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403273 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403273 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403273 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186403277 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403273 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "cade3433-2a7c-573e-ae14-9f4f0ad1cbde" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403274 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\,\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403274 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403274 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c3b7074a-75b7-5dfa-ba96-9067b0b0c2da" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403275 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\,\\frac{1}{2e}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403275 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403275 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9ca59391-4b16-5de2-b31a-e434042882de" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403276 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\,\\frac{e}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403276 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403276 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b7da2d97-ee19-5b91-aae1-d3e1ef8e41cc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403277 #edb/ref 1080 "-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403277 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403277 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c0595185-9dbe-5e61-833d-f322b3bc5d90" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403278 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\,\\frac{1}{3e}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403278 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403278 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "efa241d0-aa74-5ee0-84e5-879e44d2f438" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522901 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186522912 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186522901 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186522901 #edb/ref 1071 "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=3t e^{3t},\\quad y=5(t^2+2)e^{-3t},\\quad -\\infty<t<\\infty,\n$$\n\ncalculate $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ as a function of $t$ for $t\\ne - \\frac{1}{3}.$\n\n$\\frac{dy}{dx}=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186522901 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1aeeb45a-51fe-5f7f-b6b3-81fb614e69f4" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186522901 #edb/ref 1074 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\nx'(t)=3\\left(\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(t\\right)\\right)e^{3t}+3t\\left(\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(e^{3t}\\right)\\right),\\quad y'(t)=5\\left(\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(t^2+2\\right)\\right)e^{-3t}+5(t^2+2)\\left(\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(e^{-3t}\\right)\\right)\n$$\n\n$$\nx'(t)=3e^{3t}+ 3t(3e^{3t}),\\quad y'(t)=5(2t)e^{-3t}+5(t^2+2)(-3e^{-3t})\n$$\n\n$$\nx'(t)=3(1+3t)e^{3t},\\quad y'(t)=5(2t-3(t^2+2))e^{-3t}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{5(2t-3(t^2+2))e^{-3t}}{3(1+3t)e^{3t}}=\\frac{5(2t-3(t^2+2))}{3(1+3t)}e^{-6t}.\n$$\n\nThis derivative is defined for $t\\ne - \\frac{1}{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186522908 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186522905 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186522908 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186522908 #edb/ref 1071 "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1t}{t+1},\\quad y=\\frac{1t^2}{t+4},\\quad t>0,\n$$\n\ncalculate $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ as a function of $t.$\n\n$\\frac{dy}{dx}=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186522908 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "85e9a979-dd16-5177-b9bf-cda7e7a25733" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186522908 #edb/ref 1074 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\nx'(t)=\\frac{1\\left(\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(t\\right)\\right)(t+1)-1t\\left(\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(t+1\\right)\\right)}{(t+1)^2},\\quad y'(t)=\\frac{1\\left(\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(t^2\\right)\\right)(t+4)-1t^2\\left(\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(t+4\\right)\\right)}{(t+4)^2}\n$$\n\n$$\nx'(t)=\\frac{1(t+1)-1t(1)}{(t+1)^2},\\quad y'(t)=\\frac{2t(t+4)-1t^2(1)}{(t+4)^2}\n$$\n\n$$\nx'(t)=\\frac{1t+1-1t}{(t+1)^2},\\quad y'(t)=\\frac{2t^2+8t-1t^2}{(t+4)^2}\n$$\n\n$$\nx'(t)=\\frac{1}{(t+1)^2},\\quad y'(t)=\\frac{1t^2+8t}{(t+4)^2}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{\\frac{1t^2+8t}{(t+4)^2}}{\\frac{1}{(t+1)^2}}=\\frac{(1t^2+8t)(t+1)^2}{1(t+4)^2}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186522915 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186522914 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186522915 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186522915 #edb/ref 1071 "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=3t e^{1t},\\quad y=5(t^2+2)e^{-1t},\\quad -\\infty<t<\\infty,\n$$\n\ncalculate $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ as a function of $t$ for $t\\ne -1.$\n\n$\\frac{dy}{dx}=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186522915 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d686c858-3d09-57c7-a18a-662015e75d19" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186522915 #edb/ref 1074 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\nx'(t)=3\\left(\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(t\\right)\\right)e^{1t}+3t\\left(\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(e^{1t}\\right)\\right),\\quad y'(t)=5\\left(\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(t^2+2\\right)\\right)e^{-1t}+5(t^2+2)\\left(\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(e^{-1t}\\right)\\right)\n$$\n\n$$\nx'(t)=3e^{1t}+ 3t(1e^{1t}),\\quad y'(t)=5(2t)e^{-1t}+5(t^2+2)(-1e^{-1t})\n$$\n\n$$\nx'(t)=3(1+1t)e^{1t},\\quad y'(t)=5(2t-1(t^2+2))e^{-1t}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{5(2t-1(t^2+2))e^{-1t}}{3(1+1t)e^{1t}}=\\frac{5(2t-1(t^2+2))}{3(1+1t)}e^{-2t}.\n$$\n\nThis derivative is defined for $t\\ne -1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186522916 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186522910 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186522916 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186522916 #edb/ref 1071 "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=2t e^{1t},\\quad y=5(t^2+2)e^{-1t},\\quad -\\infty<t<\\infty,\n$$\n\ncalculate $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ as a function of $t$ for $t\\ne -1.$\n\n$\\frac{dy}{dx}=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186522916 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d8e50997-ca79-5fb3-921b-0f38c140cd4d" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186522916 #edb/ref 1074 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\nx'(t)=2\\left(\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(t\\right)\\right)e^{1t}+2t\\left(\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(e^{1t}\\right)\\right),\\quad y'(t)=5\\left(\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(t^2+2\\right)\\right)e^{-1t}+5(t^2+2)\\left(\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(e^{-1t}\\right)\\right)\n$$\n\n$$\nx'(t)=2e^{1t}+ 2t(1e^{1t}),\\quad y'(t)=5(2t)e^{-1t}+5(t^2+2)(-1e^{-1t})\n$$\n\n$$\nx'(t)=2(1+1t)e^{1t},\\quad y'(t)=5(2t-1(t^2+2))e^{-1t}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{5(2t-1(t^2+2))e^{-1t}}{2(1+1t)e^{1t}}=\\frac{5(2t-1(t^2+2))}{2(1+1t)}e^{-2t}.\n$$\n\nThis derivative is defined for $t\\ne -1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186522919 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186522913 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186522919 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186522919 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/d0/d0a61578b1ef5383e5e8e9e23c3c6309ede794d6b4f9c47a7ce8103b02f79fe2.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve (shown above)\n\n$$\nx=6\\left(2t{e}^{t}\\right),\\,y=4\\left({t}^{2}+2t\\right),\\,0\\le t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\n find the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186522919 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f38d491a-6dbf-5ea6-9e1d-28ccc7170e0f" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186522919 #edb/ref 1074 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=6\\left(2{e}^{t}(t+1)\\right),\\,{y}^{′}(t)=4\\left(2t+2\\right).\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{4\\left(2t+2\\right)}{6\\left(2{e}^{t}(t+1)\\right)}=\\frac{4\\left(1\\right)}{6\\left({e}^{t}\\right)}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=1$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{4\\left(1\\right)}{6\\left({e}^{1}\\right)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\left(1\\right)}{6\\left(e\\right)}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186522920 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186522904 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186522920 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186522920 #edb/ref 1071 "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{4t}{t+2},\\quad y=\\frac{4t^2}{t+1},\\quad t>0,\n$$\n\ncalculate $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ as a function of $t.$\n\n$\\frac{dy}{dx}=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186522920 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fb2910a3-e9dd-5491-a8ee-7d4f932f22ed" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186522920 #edb/ref 1074 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\nx'(t)=\\frac{4\\left(\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(t\\right)\\right)(t+2)-4t\\left(\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(t+2\\right)\\right)}{(t+2)^2},\\quad y'(t)=\\frac{4\\left(\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(t^2\\right)\\right)(t+1)-4t^2\\left(\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(t+1\\right)\\right)}{(t+1)^2}\n$$\n\n$$\nx'(t)=\\frac{4(t+2)-4t(1)}{(t+2)^2},\\quad y'(t)=\\frac{8t(t+1)-4t^2(1)}{(t+1)^2}\n$$\n\n$$\nx'(t)=\\frac{4t+8-4t}{(t+2)^2},\\quad y'(t)=\\frac{8t^2+8t-4t^2}{(t+1)^2}\n$$\n\n$$\nx'(t)=\\frac{8}{(t+2)^2},\\quad y'(t)=\\frac{4t^2+8t}{(t+1)^2}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{\\frac{4t^2+8t}{(t+1)^2}}{\\frac{8}{(t+2)^2}}=\\frac{(4t^2+8t)(t+2)^2}{8(t+1)^2}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186522922 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186083240.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186522922 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "48db496b-b8ed-5f24-b555-c212cdd45a54" #edb/ref 17592186045443]}
